# Supabase RLS required for schema changes

Any migration that **creates a table** (or exposes a new publicly accessible relation) must enable RLS and define policies in the **same** migration. Do not ship `CREATE TABLE` and leave RLS for a follow-up.

## Required checklist (new table)

1. `ALTER TABLE public.<table> ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;`
2. Policies for every needed command (`SELECT` / `INSERT` / `UPDATE` / `DELETE`) and role (`anon` / `authenticated` / `service_role` only if intentional).
3. Prefer ownership via `auth.uid()` and existing DB relationships (`user_id`, `home_id` → `homes`, `project_id` → `projects` / `project_owners`). Do not hardcode role/name strings for business state.
4. Idempotent policy creates: `DROP POLICY IF EXISTS ...` then `CREATE POLICY ...`.
5. Confirm with: table has RLS enabled **and** at least one policy (RLS on with zero policies blocks all non-superuser access and still fails Supabase advisors differently than RLS off).

## New columns / alters

- Adding columns to an existing RLS-protected table usually needs **no** new policy if access is still row-owner based.
- If the column changes who can read/write rows, update policies in the same migration.
- Do not disable RLS to "make inserts work" - fix policies instead.

## Examples

```sql
-- BAD: table created, RLS missing (Supabase advisor warning)
CREATE TABLE public.example_notes (
  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users (id),
  body text NOT NULL
);

-- GOOD: RLS + owner policies in the same migration
CREATE TABLE public.example_notes (
  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users (id),
  body text NOT NULL
);

ALTER TABLE public.example_notes ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY example_notes_select_own ON public.example_notes
  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (user_id = auth.uid());

CREATE POLICY example_notes_insert_own ON public.example_notes
  FOR INSERT TO authenticated
  WITH CHECK (user_id = auth.uid());

CREATE POLICY example_notes_update_own ON public.example_notes
  FOR UPDATE TO authenticated
  USING (user_id = auth.uid())
  WITH CHECK (user_id = auth.uid());

CREATE POLICY example_notes_delete_own ON public.example_notes
  FOR DELETE TO authenticated
  USING (user_id = auth.uid());
```

## Catalog / public-read tables

If authenticated (or anon) clients must read shared catalog data, still `ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` and add an explicit `FOR SELECT` policy (`USING (true)` only when intentional). Never leave catalog tables with RLS disabled.
